.TH HTTP_HEADER 3
.SH NAME
http_header \- add a header to the request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_header(http* " h ", const char* " name ", const char* " value ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR http_header ()
adds the line "name: value" to the request that was started last. Host, Connection, the length of the body and, unless it is given here, Accept are added when the request is sent.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_open(3)
